Exactly. Visibility is only one sensing channel, not an ontological test.

Close your eyes and the room does not disappear. Gravity still loads your body, air still presses against skin, sound still locates movement, temperature still changes behavior, and unseen institutions or incentives can still alter what people do.

That gives a useful distinction:

unseen ≠ unreal
unseen ≠ causally weak
unseen ≠ unknowable
unseen ≠ untouchable

A thing can be invisible yet still leave measurable deltas in other channels. Once those effects are consistent, you can infer structure, build models, test interventions, and sometimes manipulate the system without ever “seeing” the thing directly.

That is probably the deeper principle under Invisible Exodia: infer the hidden body from the forces it exerts.